<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Privacy Policy — Albany JW Parking</title>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <link href="/vendor/bootstrap/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/fontawesome/css/fontawesome.min.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/fontawesome/css/all.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/styles.css">
</head>
<body data-authed="false">

    <%- include('partials/header.ejs') %>

    <main class="container py-5 legal-container">
        <div class="legal-card">

        <h1 class="mb-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-muted small mb-4">Last updated: May 2025</p>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h5">1. About This Site</h2>
            <p>
                Albany JW Parking is a volunteer coordination platform operated by and for the
                parking team of the Albany Regional Convention of Jehovah's Witnesses. This policy
                explains what personal information we collect, how we use it, and your rights
                regarding that information.
            </p>
            <p class="text-muted small">
                This website is not sponsored, created, or controlled by Jehovah's Witnesses or
                www.JW.org, legally known as the Watch Tower Bible and Tract Society of Pennsylvania.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h5">2. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>When you register as a volunteer, we collect:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Full name</li>
                <li>Email address</li>
                <li>Phone number</li>
                <li>Date of birth</li>
                <li>Congregation name</li>
                <li>Spiritual status (elder, ministerial servant, pioneer, etc.)</li>
                <li>Notes relevant to parking assignments</li>
                <li>Crew and scheduling preferences</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We do not collect payment information, government-issued ID numbers, or any
                financial data.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h5">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <p>Your information is used solely for convention volunteer coordination:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Creating and managing your volunteer account</li>
                <li>Scheduling you for parking shifts</li>
                <li>Sending SMS and email communications about your assignments</li>
                <li>Tracking attendance at convention days</li>
                <li>Generating internal reports for parking overseers</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties for
                marketing purposes.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h5">4. Cookies</h2>
            <p>This site uses two types of strictly necessary cookies:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Session cookie</strong> (<code>connect.sid</code>) — Keeps you logged
                    in during your visit. This cookie expires when you close your browser or after
                    15 minutes of inactivity.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>CSRF cookie</strong> (<code>_csrf</code>) — Protects form submissions
                    from cross-site request forgery attacks. This is a security requirement and
                    cannot be disabled.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We do not use advertising cookies, tracking cookies, or analytics cookies.
                Because our cookies are strictly necessary for the site to function securely,
                they are set automatically upon your first visit.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h5">5. Third-Party Services</h2>
            <p>We use the following third-party services to operate the platform:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Twilio</strong> — SMS delivery. Your phone number is transmitted to
                    Twilio to send you scheduling messages. See
                    <a href="https://www.twilio.com/en-us/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Twilio's Privacy Policy</a>.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>IONOS</strong> — Email delivery. Your email address is used to
                    send you account and scheduling communications via IONOS mail servers.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Microsoft Azure</strong> — Application hosting and database storage.
                    Your data is stored in Azure SQL and served via Azure App Service.
                    See <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/en-us/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft's Privacy Statement</a>.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h5">6. Data Retention</h2>
            <p>
                Volunteer records are retained for the duration of the convention season and
                reviewed at season end. Records may be retained between seasons to simplify
                re-enrollment for returning volunteers. You may request deletion of your
                account at any time by contacting a parking administrator.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h5">7. Your Rights</h2>
            <p>You may request to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
                <li>Correct inaccurate information in your account</li>
                <li>Delete your volunteer account and associated data</li>
                <li>Opt out of SMS communications by replying STOP to any message</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                To exercise these rights, contact a parking team administrator directly or
                use the contact information available through your assigned overseer.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h5">8. Security</h2>
            <p>
                We take reasonable precautions to protect your information, including HTTPS
                encryption in transit, HttpOnly session cookies, CSRF protection on all forms,
                and role-based access controls that limit data visibility to authorized personnel.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="h5">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>
                We may update this policy periodically. Changes will be reflected by an updated
                date at the top of this page. Continued use of the site after changes are posted
                constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
            </p>
        </section>

    </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/footer.ejs') %>
    <script src="/vendor/bootstrap/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/cookieConsent.js"></script>
</body>
</html>